Relay Room
Relay Room. A switchboard with three slots stands here. A door leads north.
You can see a switchboard (in which is a beta panel) and an alpha panel here.
> board
Slots: [102 .... 0V/0 >103] [empty] [empty]. Load 1, changes 1, lookups 0.
device / panel 101: 0 uses, trail, no peer.
device / panel 102: 0 uses, trail 100 (seated first), feeds gamma.
device / panel 103: 0 uses, trail, no peer.
Score 0.
> x switchboard
Three slots: 102 empty empty. The load dial reads 1.
> x beta panel
A relay panel, code 102, at 0V. Lamps ..... It feeds the gamma panel.
> probe 102
Code 102: 0V, 0 lit, feeds 103, 1 in trail.
> probe 103
Code 103: 9V, 1 lit, 0 in trail.
> probe 104
No panel has code 104.
> tog 1 on alpha
Lamp 1 on the alpha panel is now on. 1 lit, 1 by count.
> tog 5 on alpha
The alpha panel has lamps 1 to 4.
> tog 2 on switchboard
Only panels have lamps.
> charge alpha to 7
The alpha panel reads 7V.
> charge beta to 20
The beta panel reads 12V (at the limit).
The gamma panel picks up 1V and reads 10V.
> charge switchboard to 3
That takes no charge.
> link alpha to beta
The alpha panel now feeds the beta panel.
> link beta to alpha
The beta panel now feeds the alpha panel, and is fed back.
> link alpha to alpha
The alpha panel can't feed itself.
> link alpha to switchboard
Only panels can be linked.
> note alpha
Noted 7V with 1 lit.
> note alpha
Noted 7V with 1 lit, unchanged.
> tog 2 on alpha
Lamp 2 on the alpha panel is now on. 2 lit, 2 by count.
> note alpha
Noted 7V with 2 lit, same voltage.
> charge alpha to 3
The alpha panel reads 3V.
The beta panel picks up 1V and reads 12V.
> note alpha
Noted 3V with 2 lit, lower.
> note alpha
The alpha panel has no room for another note.
> x alpha
A relay panel, code 101, at 3V. Lamps **... It feeds the beta panel. Last note 3V.
> seat alpha
The alpha panel goes into slot 2. Load 2.
> seat alpha
The alpha panel is already seated.
> seat switchboard
Only panels fit the switchboard.
